id: pm-github-quay
title: Adopt SDK 2026.11.4 contracts while retaining atomic import rollback guarantees
description: "PR 194 pins pm-cli 2026.11.4, pm-ops 2026.11.4 and pm-changelog 2026.10.31. GH-1614 plain assignments now use literal JSON input; source finalization restores the assignee after native close. Reverted-fix proof fails on undefined versus none. Full npm test: 1646 tests, 1644 pass, zero failures/cancellations, two exact SDK 2026.11.4-only pm-cli#1656 skips with all compensation assertions retained and automatic re-enable on another SDK. Typecheck/lint and strict all-source coverage pass: 14180 lines/statements, 445 functions, 5277 branches, all exactly covered across 29 authored modules. The 71-entry classification is in docs/toolchain-1104-validation.md. Atomic source-lifecycle rollback and recovered finalization still require a supported transaction-owned finalizer from pm-cli#1656. Never bypass ownership guards or claim these two skipped guarantees are certified."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[8]: ci,dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1656","gh:unbraind/pm-github#194","gh:unbraind/pm-github#197",migration,sdk,sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:17:15.200Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T06:15:42.880Z"
author: pi-glm
comments[34]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T09:27:51.980Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Reproduced the real-SDK compensation failure on the actual lockfile SDK 2026.10.28 (manifest remains >=2026.10.17). Root cause is the pm-cli 2026.10.26 GH-1591 ownership-proof hardening in src/sdk/item-transaction.ts. Before .26, compensateByRestore forced a timestamp restore. Since .26, hasOwnedCompensationEffects requires exclusive step ownership or a sibling compensation restoring the exact forward-state hash. commitGithubImportTransaction calls persistImportFidelity from its committing observer; that appends a separate import event (Preserve GitHub source lifecycle), so an ordinary subsequent observer failure correctly refuses rollback with transaction_partial_mutation rather than overwriting an unowned event. Classification: production integration depends on the former broad compensation behavior. Do not loosen the assertion or disable the SDK safety guard. Investigating a supported journaled finalizer; callback reordering or moving fidelity after commit would stop testing rollback after finalization and weaken the import guarantee."
  "2026-11-03T09:30:06.714Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Supported API review: BulkItemMutation accepts create/update/close/release, and onTransition is an observer, not a journaled custom mutation. Exact lifecycle timestamps currently require persistImportFidelity/mutateItem. No safe small production fix was found on the existing supported SDK range: post-commit finalization weakens rollback, callback reordering bypasses the failing boundary, and spoofed internal markers or force restoration bypass ownership safety. Added docs/atomic-finalization-sdk.md with versions, GH-1591 source comparison, minimal public SDK call shape, actual refusal and required journaled-finalizer support. Keep the existing regression red and report this as a production integration blocker with an upstream API requirement, not an asserted SDK regression. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-11-03T09:45:26.334Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Minimal public SDK reproducer verified on installed 2026.10.28: one bulk UPDATE, then client.update in committing, then an ordinary thrown error. Result is AggregateError compensation failed with transaction_partial_mutation; the item retains title Changed and description Source finalization, journal status compensating. This confirms the ownership-proof boundary independently of GitHub HTTP fixtures and source lifecycle timestamp handling. The synthetic tracker was removed after read-back. Typecheck and lint pass; npm test and the focused linked regression are running with the documented expected failure. Coverage/release gates were not run."
  "2026-11-03T10:04:00.584Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Final bounded gates: npm test ran build/build:test for about 34 minutes and reported 343 tests, 282 pass, zero assertion failures, 61 canceled when stopped before later files; this does not cover the known import-fidelity regression. The focused real-SDK import-fidelity regression explicitly fails with incomplete compensation, including through pm test. A separate minimal public SDK call reproduces the same transaction_partial_mutation and compensating journal. Typecheck, lint, privacy and changelog regeneration/check pass. Coverage and release:check were not run. Pushing documentation and complete diagnostic evidence only; the production finalizer integration remains blocked on a supported journaled raw lifecycle step. No assertions, ownership guards or production behavior were weakened. Coordinator should decide the upstream API request; no new upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-11-04T19:19:00.125Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Re-checking PR 194 after merging origin/main and adopting registry-confirmed pm-cli 2026.11.4, pm-ops 2026.11.4, pm-changelog 2026.10.31. Read issues 197 and 199 plus docs/atomic-finalization-sdk.md first. Preserve every compensation assertion and SDK ownership guard; verify the known failure on the current SDK before selecting a supported fix. Only focused tests run while the preceding package final coverage gate is active."
  "2026-11-04T19:23:09.230Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (production): pm-cli 2026.10.30 GH-1614 preserves typed assignee sentinel strings. normalizeImportValue erased none in assignment/sprint comparison, potentially hiding a real identity update as unchanged. New real-SDK identity regression fails 0/1 against the original source. Preserve literals, retain explicit absent/unset clears, and update exact unchanged-comparison assertions to distinguish empty and literal none values."
  "2026-11-04T19:25:15.713Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Current SDK recheck: the three existing focused compensation cases report 1 pass and 2 failures. Fresh refresh cleanup now passes; source-lifecycle rollback after finalization and recovered refresh-plan cleanup still fail with cannot safely compensate incomplete step. Classification: production integration relies on pre-GH-1591 broad rollback; the CLI ownership refusal is protective behavior, not an asserted upstream regression. Still needs pm-cli#1656 for a journaled owned lifecycle finalizer. SDK 2026.11.4 expected revision guards (GH-1576) do not extend the bulk mutation union or supply that ownership. Keep the remaining assertions unchanged."
  "2026-11-04T19:26:31.438Z",codex-toolchain-1104,Independent minimal public SDK recheck on 2026.11.4 confirms AggregateError with transaction_partial_mutation and retained compensating journal. One bulk update followed by client.update in committing and an ordinary thrown error leaves title Changed and description Source finalization instead of restoring Original. Documented exact remaining #1656 requirement without asserting the protective refusal itself is a CLI regression. Corrected sentinel/unchanged comparison tests pass 19/19.
  "2026-11-04T19:31:23.209Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Explicitly reverted only import-fidelity.ts to origin/main, confirmed the new real-SDK typed-identity test fails 0/1 (empty versus literal none), and restored the fix. Corrected focused identity/scheduled-refusal tests pass 19/19, and the linked sentinel test rerun passes. Typecheck and lint pass. Atomic lifecycle rollback and recovered refresh cleanup remain unchanged failing acceptance cases pending #1656."
  "2026-11-04T19:45:56.072Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Verified auxiliary gates on fix commit 065d3f8: typecheck, lint, privacy (8569 local objects), docstrings (28 files, 269 declarations), production dependency audit (zero vulnerabilities), changelog regeneration/check, and zero-duplication gate pass. dist is not tracked in this repository; built it for artifact acceptance. Only package.json/package-lock.json carry current development pins; current explanatory docs separate minimums from the independent pin and retain dated historical receipts. Full npm test will run serially after the preceding package coverage attempt ends."
  "2026-11-04T20:01:26.371Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (test): SDK 2026.10.30 GH-1614 rejects typed parent: none. Focused baselines: discussion-model 0/1, discussions 0/16, labels 3/13, label-import-model 0/3; the targeted 500-native-comma project writer also fails at its root fixture. Converted only those explicit resets to unset parent, merging it into existing unset lists. Existing hierarchy assignments, 500-sequence/native-tag models, preservation assertions and exact counts remain intact. Updated shared fixture, packed acceptance and manual validation companions consistently; the minimum-host probe now uses the portable explicit unset too."
  "2026-11-04T20:06:22.288Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"After fixture migration, the representative native discussion/label cases pass 2/2, build:test and lint pass, and the full exact-minimum consumer passes 1/1 again with explicit unset parent on SDK 2026.10.17. The longer focused 500-sequence batch was interrupted before completion to keep only one heavy suite active; it is not claimed passing. Full inventory remains queued for the serial npm test run."
  "2026-11-04T20:25:39.259Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (test): pm-changelog 2026.10.31 entry Fail closed when requested release notes have no matching section (pmc-pending-version-notes) now rejects an explicitly requested release that was suppressed as empty. changelog-placement.test.ts creates an intentionally empty September tag and requests that version while testing an October Unreleased delivery. Baseline is 3/5, with both tagged variants refusing MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE. Add the documented include-empty opt-in to that fixture caller script, retain every Unreleased/non-backfill assertion, and strengthen the tagged case to require exactly one visible empty historical section. No production workflow flags or guard semantics are changed."
  "2026-11-04T20:36:24.428Z",codex-toolchain-1104,The corrected changelog-placement file now passes 5/5 on Node 26.13.0. The intentionally empty September release is explicitly admitted with include-empty and asserted visible exactly once with the renderer empty body No changes.; October delivery remains Unreleased in both workflow variants. The full run had already loaded the prior fixture and records its two old failures; this focused receipt verifies their repair. Existing production workflow flags and every original placement/status/custom-script assertion are retained.
  "2026-11-04T20:41:27.014Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Additional test contract migration under pm-changelog 2026.10.31: closeout-workflow.test.ts had a flat caller generator receiving no-pending-release without all-release-tags. The documented historical-only exception requires both; otherwise an absent explicitly requested release is refused. Three focused workflow cases reproduced 0/3 with MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE, independently of the existing host/Git-advice note pm-github-gaq8. Add all-release-tags to that fixture caller only, preserving the malicious-content scan, zero-close cleanup, read-denial annotation and behavioral-revert assertions. Untagged placement already verifies the documented suppression, so no upstream regression is asserted."
  "2026-11-04T20:49:47.712Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"pm-changelog 2026.10.31 test contract: the workflow caller fixture requested historical-only notes via --no-pending-release without --all-release-tags. Three baseline privacy/zero-close/read-denial cases all failed with MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE before reaching their assertions. Match the documented historical-only exception by adding --all-release-tags to the fixture caller. Five focused cases now pass, including zero-close drift refusal and the staged-privacy behavioral revert; all assertions remain intact. This is separate from the older host-Git diagnosis and is not an established pm-cli regression."
  "2026-11-04T20:54:27.571Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Remaining production GH-1614 mismatch: current plain repeat-import file reproduced 0/1 at seed 17, with an updated_at-only durable change on the second identical import. The plain writer still passes --assignee none to pm update/create, while the typed comparator preserves the literal GitHub identity. A standalone SDK 2026.11.4 probe confirms CLI update --assignee none removes the field, but typed update({assignee: \"none\"}) stores \"none\". This is a production integration defect, not evidence for another upstream regression. Keep exact snapshot/no-op assertions; the remaining plain writer migration is not certified within this run budget."
  "2026-11-04T20:54:35.358Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Bounded full validation: Node 26 npm test ran 2019884 ms before an explicit local-budget SIGINT. Runner totals: 648 tests, 577 pass, 21 fail, 50 cancelled, 0 skipped. The actual assertions were two empty-release placement refusals, eighteen historical-only workflow refusals, and one plain repeat-import no-op failure. Changelog fixtures had already loaded their old definitions: corrected placement file now passes 5/5 and five representative corrected workflow cases pass 5/5, including privacy and behavioral-revert checks; the complete repaired workflow file was not rerun. Separate atomic-finalization matrix remains 1 pass/2 fail awaiting pm-cli#1656. No full coverage gate was run because the suite remains red and the repo budget expired. Final build:test, typecheck, lint, strict health and privacy pass; thresholds, ignores and compensation assertions are unchanged. This is a partial verified migration, not a green release gate."
  "2026-11-04T20:55:26.327Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Final pin audit: test/discussion-packed-acceptance.ts advertised current npm/Bun hosts but hard-coded SDK 2026.10.28 in three installs and its receipt. Derive those four values from the exact declared devDependency, now 2026.11.4, so future group bumps stay consistent. Historical reproduction documents and imported issue fixtures retain their observed versions; the minimum consumer intentionally retains SDK 2026.10.17. The packed discussion script is compiled and linted but its five-host runtime matrix was not rerun within the repo budget."
  "2026-11-04T21:00:34.094Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Resume authorized for PR 194 only. Worktree is clean at e1be8be. Plan: fix the plain GH-1614 writer with real repeat-import regression and reverted-fix proof; rerun the previously failed/cancelled cases, inspect existing skip support for the independently proven pm-cli#1656 cases, preserve every compensation assertion, then complete a serial nice full-suite run and typecheck/lint. Run coverage only after green tests. Do not touch PR 87 or close issues 197/199."
  "2026-11-04T21:06:06.584Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"GH-1614 production fix: plain create/update now feed assignment values through --stdin-json instead of sentinel-bearing --assignee/--sprint flags. Native close clears assignee, so plain source finalization restores the explicit source identity while link-only owners remain untouched. New real plain-writer regression covers existing updates, fresh creates, open/closed sources, none/null assignees and milestone names, exact readback and byte-identical repeat imports. Reverting both production files makes the new regression fail 0/1; restored code passes literal plus complete daily-idempotency files 5/5, including all generated seeds."
  "2026-11-04T21:06:08.384Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Fresh SDK 2026.11.4 finalization recheck remains exactly 1 pass and 2 failures. Existing repo test options already support reason-bearing Node skip (privacy/gate POSIX and root-permission fixtures). Under the new authorization, skip only the source-lifecycle compensation case and recovered=true terminal refresh case, each citing pm-cli#1656. Every assertion remains in place; fresh refresh compensation still executes. Skips are conditional on installed SDK version 2026.11.4 so a new SDK release automatically re-enables both cases for re-evaluation. No production ownership or rollback guard is bypassed."
  "2026-11-04T21:08:36.140Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Ready for full rerun: corrected literal and daily-idempotency files 5/5; reverted-fix control 0/1; linked new plain regression 1/1. Minimum packed consumer 1/1 with actual floor CLI JSON input; exact finalization matrix now 1 pass/2 explicit pm-cli#1656 skips, zero failures. Prior report inventory is exactly 71 entries: 2 empty-release assertions, 18 historical-only workflow assertions, 1 plain-import assertion, and 50 budget cancellations. Complete npm test will rerun every previously failed/cancelled file and supply the per-entry classification; budget cancellations are not host-load timeouts."
  "2026-11-04T21:10:17.488Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"First full command stopped in build:test before executing tests: the new regression treated generic list metadata tags as a typed array (TS2339). Narrow tags with Array.isArray before finding the exact provenance tag; runtime assertions are unchanged. Test compilation now passes. Restart the full command; do not count the compile-only attempt as a completed test suite."
  "2026-11-04T21:37:12.015Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Full rerun progress: all twenty original changelog-related assertions have now emitted passing results (2 placement and 18 workflow). The real workflow safety, no-op behavioral-revert and peer-writer lease assertions remain intact. The discussion model worker has finished and the second worker has advanced; its outcome remains buffered behind the workflow file and is not yet certified. Keep the full run uninterrupted; no host-load timeout classification has been inferred from the old deliberate SIGINT cancellations."
  "2026-11-04T22:18:43.445Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Full rerun milestone: all 186 closeout decision-matrix rows pass. Exact title matching against the prior failure inventory confirms all 21 original failed assertions now emit passes: 2 empty requested releases, 18 historical-only workflow fixtures, and the plain repeat-import property. More than 1000 checks have emitted successful results; the full command is still processing the remaining files, so do not certify completion or coverage yet. The source-lifecycle case has emitted its explicit pm-cli#1656 skip reason; the recovered refresh case is still later in the queue."
  "2026-11-04T22:40:34.751Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Completed full Node 26 npm test on source head 8b11727: 1646 tests, 1644 pass, 0 fail, 0 cancelled, exactly 2 skips, 0 todo, duration 5277066 ms. Both skips are the previously reproduced pm-cli#1656 cases; the fresh-refresh compensation case executes and passes. Every one of the 21 original assertion failures now emits a passing result, and all 50 previously cancelled file entries were included in the completed 72-file run. No host-load timeout occurred, so none is classified that way. All 186 workflow decision rows and the 500-sequence models remain intact. Typecheck and lint follow the full run; coverage is authorized only after these succeed."
  "2026-11-05T01:42:49.038Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Coverage gate completed with exit 0: all 29 authored modules, exact 14180/14180 lines and statements, 445/445 functions, 5277/5277 branches, zero skipped source entries and unchanged four 100-percent thresholds. Instrumented test phase: 1646 tests, 1644 pass, zero failures/cancellations, the same two pm-cli#1656 skips, 7936886 ms. Native merge kept all 3883 receipts; no pre-filter, ignore or assertion weakening. Full 71-entry classification is documented. Coverage alone took about three hours, so the follow-up exceeded the approximate time estimate rather than stopping another required run early."
  "2026-11-05T01:45:49.409Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Final additional gates pass: docstrings document all 269 declarations in 28 files; duplication gate reports zero duplicated lines across 29 authored modules; regenerated changelog and changelog check are unchanged and pass after fetching tags. Runtime sources, manifest and dependency files are byte-identical to tested source head 8b11727; remaining changes are validation documentation and PM evidence only. Release claims without closing items; verify strict health, commit identity and privacy before the final non-force push."
  "2026-11-05T04:28:01.994Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Reviewer follow-up authorized for PR 194 only. Clean worktree at 8907c14; existing gate predicates still quarantine exactly installed SDK 2026.11.4. Add fixture-version tests that execute each actual predicate and skip expression and fail under widened/inverted mutations, add an existing-owner update-then-close assignee restoration regression with reverted-restore proof, and document the known lifecycle-finalization limitation in README. Preserve all compensation assertions, existing quarantine scope, and disabled auto-merge. Run the requested complete nice npm test, then typecheck/lint; do not repeat completed coverage or dependency migration."
  "2026-11-05T04:31:36.249Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Reviewer condition 1: test/atomic-finalization-quarantine.test.ts evaluates the actual predicates AND skip options in both compensation test files against 12 fixture versions, without installing SDKs. Only exact 2026.11.4 is waived; every other fixture version re-enables assertions, and fresh refresh invocation never skips. All six deliberate always-skip, inverted-predicate and skip-bypass mutations fail assertions. This is an expiring waiver allowlist, not a claim that other versions implement the missing API."
  "2026-11-05T04:31:37.787Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Reviewer condition 2: added a separate existing-owner closed-source GH-1614 regression. It proves zero creates and one update, the same owner is closed, native history orders update then close (removing assignee) then import (restoring literal none), and title and sprint survive. Removing only the existing-owner sourceAssignee argument makes the regression fail (undefined versus none); the production fix is restored. Focused five-test run and test compilation pass."
  "2026-11-05T04:31:38.710Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Reviewer condition 3 / known limitation: README now states that on pm-cli >=2026.10.26 without transaction-owned finalization (pm-cli#1656), failure after lifecycle finalization can leave partially applied state; the ownership guard refuses unsafe rollback and the recovery journal resumes the same import. It names the exact lifecycle-compensation and recovered-refresh tests quarantined only on 2026.11.4, with automatic re-enable for any other version. No compensation assertion, runtime source, minimum SDK, dependency pin or auto-merge setting was changed."
  "2026-11-05T06:15:37.816Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Reviewer follow-up final validation on Node 26.13.0: NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null nice -n 10 npm test completed with 1649 tests: 1647 passed, 0 failed, 0 cancelled, 2 skipped, duration 6167670.956242 ms. The two fixture-version quarantine tests and existing-owner update-close-restore regression pass within the complete suite. All seven deliberate mutations were rejected, then restored before this run. Only the exact two unchanged pm-cli#1656 compensation cases skip on installed SDK 2026.11.4. Sequential nice npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run changelog:check all pass after fetching tags; changelog unchanged. No coverage rerun for this test/documentation-only follow-up; earlier coverage receipts remain scoped to their recorded source head. Runtime sources, pins, compensation assertions and auto-merge configuration unchanged. Remaining upstream requirement: transaction-owned finalization with durable recovery and compensation, pm-cli#1656 (confirmed open)."
